## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Increase number of concurrent ports/sockets
##+Q 65536

## Tweak GC to run more often
##-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## EPMD-less distribution, for every release.
## Uses a custom EPMD module (EvoGit.EpmdDist) that resolves remote node ports
## from a registry populated at runtime by EvoGit.RemoteConnection when an
## SSH tunnel is opened. Local dashboard releases do NOT start distribution at
## boot — it is enabled on-demand via EvoGit.Distribution.
-start_epmd false
-epmd_module Elixir.EvoGit.EpmdDist
-dist_listen true

<%= if @release.name == :genesis_server do %>
## genesis_server deliberately sets NO inet_dist_listen_* range here.
## As an SSH remote-dev daemon its listen port is PINNED AT LAUNCH by
## GENESIS_REMOTE_DIST_PORT (rel/env.sh.eex → ELIXIR_ERL_OPTIONS), while a
## plain dashboard server keeps OTP's ephemeral port. A range in this file
## takes precedence over ELIXIR_ERL_OPTIONS (and a second -kernel flag cannot
## override an earlier key), which would silently defeat the pin and break the
## SSH tunnel forwarding to that port.
<% else %>
## Local Dashboard — fixed distribution port range for SSH tunneling to
## remote nodes (distribution itself is enabled on demand, see above).
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 9100 inet_dist_listen_max 9200
<% end %>

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Desktop Optimization Flags
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Disable Scheduler Busy-Waiting (Saves battery and background CPU)
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none

## Process/atom limits are deliberately NOT set — the VM uses its OTP defaults.
## Capping them (+P/+t) caused atom-table exhaustion and a silent, zero-log boot failure.
